  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A diatomic ideal gas is used in a Carnot engine as the working substance. If during the adiabatic expansion part of the cycle, the volume of the gas increases from <math><mi>V</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>32</mn><mi>V</mi></math>. The efficiency of the engine is&nbsp;</p>\r"
  },
  "options": [
    {
